Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: The Green Flash Splinters the Roundabout
- Story & Context: On a blistering July afternoon in 1976, dissident technician Lennox "Wireman" Baptiste cracked open a municipal controller at the Queen's Park Savannah junction, jamming the signal lanterns into an endless, blinding emerald beacon that caused a four-mile automotive standoff. The midday air reeked of diesel exhaust and fried plantains as Clara Des Vignes leapt atop an immobilized Leyland bus, trilling a frantic concert flute melody that completely drowned out the police whistles while the crowd took up the jubilant chant, "Drive the amber down into the ditch!" Within twenty minutes, the entire gridlock surrendered its horns to the rhythm, turning an illegal union blockade into the first documented performance of the new sound.
