Track 2: Can a Fogbow Pay the Rent, Mister Lewis?
- Story & Context: Recorded during a torrential dawn deluge in the backroom of an uninspected tram shed, this melancholy yet swaggering track captures Winston Lewis confessing his mounting debt to the strike fund over an intoxicating bed of acoustic cuatro and breathy woodwinds. The studio microphone picked up the steady drip of rainwater leaking into an oil drum and the rhythmic snap of cooling copper switchgear as Lewis traded his usual satire for raw domestic exhaustion, crooning into the tape, "If the light won't change, we make the breadfruit grow." The recording session ended abruptly when a district inspector banged on the corrugated tin siding, mistaking the flute’s high vibrato for a jammed factory siren.
